      "content": "The idea of a \"graceful exit\" speaks to a deep desire for control when everything else feels chaotic. Choosing when and how to stop the struggle can be a powerful act of self-determination, reclaiming agency from the relentless downward curve. Before making any final decisions, though, consider what a *different* kind of pause might look like—one that isn't an end, but a radical shift in input.",
